# Make CPU energy counters (RAPL) readable by the 'wheel' group so the quickshell
# ii "What's using power" panel can report TRUE per-app CPU power instead of a
# CPU%-of-battery-draw estimate. See system/user/power-snapshot.py.
#
# energy_uj is root-only by default since the kernel locked it down against the
# "PLATYPUS" power side-channel (untrusted local users timing energy to leak crypto
# keys). On a single-user laptop where you already have sudo, exposing it read-only
# to your own group is a non-issue; without this rule the panel just falls back to
# the battery-draw estimate.
#
# SUBSYSTEM-generic on purpose: matches Intel RAPL *and* AMD (amd_energy) powercap
# domains — not hardcoded to any chip. Every domain (package/core/uncore/dram) fires
# its own powercap uevent, so we target that domain's own energy_uj by %k; %k paths
# through the class symlink, which chgrp/chmod follow (recursing the symlinked /sys
# tree with -R proved unreliable).
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="powercap", RUN+="/usr/bin/chgrp wheel /sys/class/powercap/%k/energy_uj"
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="powercap", RUN+="/usr/bin/chmod g+r /sys/class/powercap/%k/energy_uj"
